---

Third-party components bundled or referenced by this repository keep their own
licenses:

- services/stt — a MekaHime-modified SenseVoiceSmall service. Upstream code:
  SenseVoice (FunAudioLLM) and FunASR, MIT License (see
  services/stt/LICENSE-SenseVoice). The small SenseVoiceSmall support files in
  services/stt/models/ (tokenizer, BPE model, CMVN stats, config) and the
  model.pt weights downloaded by scripts/download_sensevoice.py are from the
  iic/SenseVoiceSmall release under the FunASR Model Open Source License
  Agreement.
- vendor/tts-engine — the OpenSakura voice server, a MekaHime build of
  GPT-SoVITS. main.py is MekaHime code under the MIT License above. It runs on
  upstream GPT-SoVITS (RVC-Boss, MIT License), which scripts/setup_tts.py
  downloads at a pinned commit together with public pretrained models, nltk
  data and ffmpeg, each under its own license (see
  vendor/tts-engine/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md); none of those files are in this
  repository. Sakura's voice model, fine-tuned weights and reference audio are
  MekaHime Inc. assets distributed separately (gated Hugging Face repository
  MekaHime/MekaHime_Sakura) for personal, hobbyist use only: no
  distillation, training, extraction, resale or commercial use.
- web/assets/avatar.vrm — Sakura's character model, created with VRoid Studio
  (pixiv) and owned by MekaHime Inc. Its embedded VRM meta states the terms:
  anyone may use her as an avatar, credit is required, personal profit is
  allowed, redistribution and modification are allowed. Sakura's design, name
  and likeness are © MekaHime Inc. and covered by the character license in the
  About tab of the web page (web/index.html), not by the MIT license above.
- web/assets/clips/*.glb — body-motion clips, CC0 1.0 (public domain): derived
  from Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 and KayKit Character
  Animations, both CC0, plus gestures keyed by MekaHime on top of them and
  dedicated to the public domain as well. See web/assets/clips/LICENSE.txt.
- three.js and @pixiv/three-vrm — MIT License, loaded from CDN.
